================================================================================
## Fix Select All in the Add Data Assets dialog
================================================================================

Context: Select All (toolbar button and header checkbox) looked like a no-op.
It forced already-loaded rows off, then the header checkbox snapped back to
unchecked/indeterminate because not every visible row was selected. The
remaining-slot count also used already-loaded flags from the current schema
listing instead of how many assets are in the domain.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-metadata.js
   Added `computeSelectAllImportState`: Select All checks every visible row,
   including Already loaded. The import-limit cap applies only to new assets
   and shows a warning when some new rows are skipped. `_remainingImportSlots`
   uses the domain metadata table count. Import submits only new tables so
   already-loaded checks do not consume the limit.
2. tests/units/front/test_add_data_assets_dialog.py
   Node tests for Select All / Deselect All / remaining-slot cap.

