## Faster Data Assets paint: deferred Rights + reload spinner
================================================================================

Context: The Unity Catalog Data Assets page felt slow to display because SELECT
permission probes ran with metadata load. After Add/Update from the popup, the
list also refreshed without a clear loading state. The heading still said
"Loaded Tables".

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_metadata.html
   Renamed "Loaded Tables" to "Loaded Unity Catalog Assets". Added
   `#metadataListOverlay` spinner over the assets table.
2. src/front/static/domain/css/domain-metadata.css
   Overlay styles for the reload spinner.
3. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-metadata.js
   - `loadMetadataStatus` paints the list first, then calls
     `refreshSelectPermissionsInBackground()`.
   - New `POST /domain/metadata/check-select` fills the Rights column in place.
   - After Add/Update (popup close / Update from UC), shows the list overlay
     spinner while reloading assets.
4. src/back/core/databricks/uc/MetadataService.py
   Import no longer probes SELECT (sets `can_select: null`). Added
   `probe_select_permissions` for the background Rights pass.
5. src/back/objects/domain/_metadata_select.py (new)
   Orchestrates the background probe + session save (kept out of Domain to
   respect the class size budget).
6. src/api/routers/internal/domain.py
   Added `POST /metadata/check-select`.
7. docs/user-guide.md
   Notes two-phase list paint + background Rights.
8. tests/units/front/test_loaded_uc_assets_deferred_rights.py (new)
   plus MetadataService / guard-UI contract updates.

